{"title":"2014 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a fixed odd prime. A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-tuple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/2079c5cb69b4e0ae84bb48eb8fca62470cddc84d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,a_3,\\ldots,a_p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> of integers is said to be good if \n</p><p>(i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba3bf0e728879a5e82615d973abc9412c279a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le a_i\\le p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and\n(ii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2d6029fc0920eb54bc462d57016e9b1f07186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+a_3+\\cdots+a_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"15\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and \n(iii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1541d7d077d5ab01925c27382150c014515353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1a_2+a_2a_3+a_3a_4+\\cdots+a_pa_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"244\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Determine the number of good <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-tuples.     \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 61/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 447/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1805/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.303      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    5.303      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25909:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234815 and revision id 205988. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}